WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.853 --> 00:00:17.005
For the next few weeks, the children happily explored outdoors.

2
00:00:18.126 --> 00:00:21.229
Now that they were living in the country, they had stopped going to school.

3
00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.852
Mother was mostly in her room, writing stories.

4
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:29.276
She sold stories for money because she said the family was poor now.

5
00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:35.110
The children still had nice clothes and there was enough to eat, so they didn't mind.

6
00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.652
They did not forget their father, but they had stopped talking about him.

7
00:00:40.632 --> 00:00:42.713
They knew such talk made Mother unhappy.

8
00:00:45.794 --> 00:00:47.515
In June it rained for three days.

9
00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.976
It was very cold, and nobody went outside.

10
00:00:52.277 --> 00:00:53.798
One day they went up to Mother's room.

11
00:00:53.818 --> 00:00:56.379
"Can we light a fire?"

12
00:00:56.679 --> 00:00:57.359
Bobbie asked.

13
00:00:57.379 --> 00:00:59.220
"It's freezing!"

14
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.461
"I'm sorry, Bobbie, coal is too expensive," Mother replied.

15
00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:09.162
"But Mother, we only need a little coal to make a fire!"

16
00:01:09.443 --> 00:01:10.083
Bobbie pleaded.

17
00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:12.123
"We can't afford it!"

18
00:01:12.523 --> 00:01:13.003
said Mother.

19
00:01:13.023 --> 00:01:14.944
"Please run along.

20
00:01:15.864 --> 00:01:16.524
I'm busy."

21
00:01:16.544 --> 00:01:21.286
"Mother is always busy," Phyllis whispered to Peter.

22
00:01:22.206 --> 00:01:22.826
Peter shrugged.

23
00:01:23.726 --> 00:01:24.387
He was thinking.

24
00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:29.028
After tea Peter told his sisters, "I have an idea."

25
00:01:30.008 --> 00:01:30.909
"What's your idea?"

26
00:01:31.249 --> 00:01:31.849
Bobbie asked.

27
00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:35.071
"I won't tell you," was Peter's answer.

28
00:01:35.091 --> 00:01:37.972
"Oh, very well," said Bobbie.

29
00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:40.794
"Don't then," Phyllis said.

30
00:01:40.814 --> 00:01:42.755
"We don't care."

31
00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:48.518
Peter looked angry and said, "There's a reason why I won't tell you.

32
00:01:49.579 --> 00:01:51.100
My idea might be wrong."

33
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.422
"Don't do it if it's wrong," Bobbie replied.

34
00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:58.704
"No," said Peter, "I'm going to do it.

35
00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.241
Some people might think it's wrong, but I don't think it is.

36
00:02:03.301 --> 00:02:08.623
If Mother asks where I am, tell her I'm playing a game called 'coal mining.'"

37
00:02:09.683 --> 00:02:13.184
Two days later Peter said, "Come quickly, and bring the pram!"

38
00:02:15.525 --> 00:02:18.245
Earlier they had seen an old pram in a shed behind the house.

39
00:02:19.386 --> 00:02:21.806
The girls got it and followed Peter to the train station.

40
00:02:22.987 --> 00:02:26.968
On the hill above the station, there was a small pile of coal in the grass.

41
00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.601
"I just found the coal," said Peter.

42
00:02:30.621 --> 00:02:33.143
"Help me carry it to the house."

43
00:02:34.964 --> 00:02:39.426
Bobbie, Peter, and Phyllis packed the pram full of coal and made three trips to the house.

44
00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:43.048
They put the coal in the pile by the back door.

45
00:02:44.249 --> 00:02:45.789
Afterward Peter went out alone.

46
00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.991
He came back dirty and looking mysterious.

47
00:02:50.632 --> 00:02:53.474
Peter went out every night, and the children told nobody.

48
00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.375
A week later Mrs.

49
00:02:55.435 --> 00:02:57.756
Viney said that there was more coal than she thought.

50
00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:03.251
The children were very happy—so happy they forgot Peter's actions might be wrong.

51
00:03:05.192 --> 00:03:08.314
Then came the awful night when the stationmaster hid in the shadows.

52
00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.677
He watched Peter climb onto the coal pile.

53
00:03:11.697 --> 00:03:13.958
"Now I've caught you, thief!"

54
00:03:14.438 --> 00:03:15.619
shouted the stationmaster.

55
00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:17.801
He grabbed Peter's jacket.

56
00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:20.062
"Come with me to the station!"

57
00:03:20.082 --> 00:03:25.145
"I'm not a thief," said Peter, but his voice shook.

58
00:03:25.166 --> 00:03:27.307
"The police station?"

59
00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:28.488
said another voice.

60
00:03:29.588 --> 00:03:30.629
The voice was Bobbie's.

61
00:03:31.649 --> 00:03:33.570
Bobbie and Phyllis stepped out of the darkness.

62
00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:36.992
"It was our fault too," Bobbie said.

63
00:03:38.673 --> 00:03:39.954
The stationmaster looked at them.

64
00:03:39.974 --> 00:03:42.775
"You're all from the white house on the hill.

65
00:03:43.816 --> 00:03:45.176
Why are you stealing coal?"

66
00:03:45.537 --> 00:03:46.017
he asked.

67
00:03:46.037 --> 00:03:48.498
"I didn't think it was stealing.

68
00:03:49.559 --> 00:03:51.780
There's so much coal here," said Peter.

69
00:03:52.881 --> 00:03:55.202
"Mother says we're too poor to have a fire."

70
00:03:56.843 --> 00:04:00.581
The stationmaster thought for a minute and said, "I won't do anything this time.

71
00:04:01.562 --> 00:04:04.084
But remember, this is the railway's coal.

72
00:04:04.724 --> 00:04:06.725
Taking the coal is stealing."

73
00:04:07.806 --> 00:04:08.647
The children nodded.

74
00:04:09.407 --> 00:04:10.248
They knew he was right.
